I fixed ROI calculations in {{etl_delivery_campaigns_ab_scorecard_lcs}}  and added few metrics to it while doing it:

* {{campaign_roi}} - now correctly reflects ROI, meaning that it’s an increase in revenues divided by campaign costs (bolt costs) -> {{order_earnings_eur_uplift / bolt_costs_uplift}}
* increased revenues include HP uplift in case p-value for GMV uplift during HP is <0.05 -> {{order_earnings_eur_uplift + order_earnings_eur_uplift_hp}} / {{bolt_costs_uplift}}
* {{campaign_roi_total_cost}} - same as ROI, but divided by {{total_cost_uplift}}
* {{order_earnings_eur = commission_fee + delivery_fee + small_order_fee + service_fee - courier_earnings}}
* {{order_earnings_eur_uplift}} - uplift of previous value
* {{order_earnings_eur_uplift_hp}} - uplift of previous value during HP

