Adding new context for reference:

When updated the filter for {{order-event}} queue, we hit the filter complexity constraint of 150: [https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/subscription-filter-policy-constraints.html|https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/subscription-filter-policy-constraints.html|smart-link].

Therefore, it was decided to split {{marketplace-kafka-order-event}} SQS queue into four queues (a separate queue for each type of {{order-event}}):

* {{marketplace-kafka-order-event-order-created}}
* {{marketplace-kafka-order-event-order-try-driver-did-not-respond}}
* {{marketplace-kafka-order-event-order-try-driver-rejected}}
* {{marketplace-kafka-order-event-order-try-waiting-driver-confirmation}}

