Hey, [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7], I guess we will discuss more later today, but:

{quote}the data will be used only for training the model?{quote}

No, we would use this view simply to backfill our new storage system.

In a nutshell: this data is already stored in a MySQL database. We want to keep our own copy of the data in an Elasticsearch index. Once the backfill is done, the data will be used to serve textual search delivery location suggestions to eaters, as well as to retrieve courier notes associated to a particular address.

See the diagram from Section 4 for more details: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4384917204/2023+Apr+-+Replace+delivery+location+with+predicted+entrance+for+Eaters#4.-Solution|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4384917204/2023+Apr+-+Replace+delivery+location+with+predicted+entrance+for+Eaters#4.-Solution|smart-link]: “Delivery Orders ES” and “Delivery Order Intent ES” are the indices we are looking to backfill. 

{quote}is data encrypted at rest and in transit{quote}

At rest - no. In transit - our backfill script could probably be written as to use HTTPS. Once the backfill is done the data will flow through the usual Bolt Node.js infra. The ES cluster is only accessible inside our VPN and access is managed by SRE.

{quote}and what would be the data retention policy.{quote}

We will hold order data for 6 months. “Order Intent” data will have the same retention policy as the {{delivery-user}} MySQL table, which I guess is indefinite. Would be good to understand if there’s something we need to do wrt data deletion requests here.

