{noformat}…
            response = await this.apiHelper
                .get(parsedInstrument.provider_method as PaymentInstrumentType)
                .authorise(ctx, req);
        } catch (e) {
            // all authorise errors come here. we wrap them into ErrorResult
            response = {
                result: {
                    type: ResultType.ERROR,
                    error: {
                        code: e instanceof BoltError ? e.code : CommonResponseCodes.SERVER_ERROR,
                        message: e instanceof Error ? e.message : "Unknown error type.",
                    },
                },
                provider_metadata: undefined,
            };
        }{noformat}

ie. if we instead of “throw exception in payment-provider => turn into ERROR result in payment-core => process the ERROR result in payment-core” do “return ERROR result from payment-provider => process the ERROR result in payment-core” should have no impact.

